# Trivy ignore list for the contextmatrix-agent worker-image scan.
#
# The worker-image-scan job fails on CRITICAL/HIGH vulnerabilities that have an
# upstream fix (ignore-unfixed: true). Every entry must carry a justification;
# review on each worker-image / Go-dependency bump and delete entries whose fix
# has shipped. Dependabot tracks the Go modules, GitHub Actions and base images;
# the yq, Task, gh, Node and npm pins are bumped by hand (see Dockerfile.worker).

# --- The yq v4.54.1 (/usr/local/bin/yq) and Task v3.54.0 (/usr/local/bin/task)
# binaries are prebuilt upstream releases compiled with Go 1.27.1 and
# golang.org/x/net v0.59.0. Both are the latest releases; only their upstream
# release pipelines can rebuild them. yq links no net/http or crypto/tls code
# and makes no network calls. Task runs no server; it reaches the network only
# to fetch remote Taskfiles (http, https or git includes), and without a TTY it
# refuses an unpinned remote Taskfile unless run with --yes or a trusted host.
# CVE-2026-111943: x509 intermediate denylist; exposes only Task's https fetch.
# CVE-2026-78667: Range-header DoS in http.ServeContent; neither serves HTTP.
# CVE-2026-78669: HTTP/2 CPU DoS; exposes only Task's remote-Taskfile fetch.
# CVE-2026-97031: ECH memory DoS in a TLS server; neither runs a TLS server.
# Clears when yq and Task both ship release builds on Go >= 1.27.3 and
# golang.org/x/net >= 0.60.0.
CVE-2026-111943
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# --- Task v3.54.0 (/usr/local/bin/task) links go-jose v4.1.4 through
# hashicorp/go-getter's GCS getter (cloud.google.com/go/storage, grpc,
# go-spiffe). CVE-2026-116587 (CPU DoS parsing a crafted RSA JWK, fixed in
# 4.1.6) needs a JWK parse on that path; Task forces a git:: source on
# go-getter, so the GCS getter never runs. Task v3.54.0 is the latest release
# - clears when a Task release links go-jose >= 4.1.6.
CVE-2026-116587

# --- The bundled npm CLI (12.2.1, the worker's pin and the latest release)
# ships undici 6.29.0 (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici); the
# fixes are in 6.29.1. Only node-gyp's header download uses it - npm's registry
# client runs on minipass-fetch. CVE-2026-109869 (DoS via an unhandled stream
# error) and CVE-2026-87018 (crash on a TLS 1.2 renegotiation to a mismatched
# certificate) need a hostile header server; the worst case is one failed
# native-addon build on the single-tenant worker. CVE-2026-109383 (Agent drops
# a function-valued tls option such as checkServerIdentity) needs a tls
# callback, and node-gyp passes TLS settings only through connect, requestTls
# and proxyTls. Clears when an npm release bundles undici >= 6.29.1.
CVE-2026-109869
CVE-2026-87018
CVE-2026-109383

# --- The uv-managed CPython (/opt/python) bundles pip, whose _vendor tree pins
# msgpack==1.1.2 and setuptools==70.3.0 (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt - Trivy reads
# the pins as installed packages). GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack Unpacker-reuse
# out-of-bounds read, fixed in 1.2.1) touches only pip's deserialization of its
# own local HTTP cache. CVE-2026-114613 (map-deserialization memory leak, fixed
# in 1.2.3) lives in msgpack's C extension; pip vendors only the pure-Python
# fallback. CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools PackageIndex path traversal, fixed in
# 78.1.1) lives in package_index.py, which pip's vendored copy does not ship -
# only the pkg_resources subset of setuptools is vendored. The pins cannot be
# raised independently of pip, and the latest pip (26.2.2) still carries both -
# clears when a pip release re-vendors msgpack >= 1.2.3 and setuptools
# >= 78.1.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2026-114613
CVE-2025-47273

# --- The same pip vendor tree pins urllib3==2.7.0; the fixes land in 2.8.0.
# CVE-2026-97687 (HTTPS-proxy TLS configuration override) needs a configured
# HTTPS proxy, which the worker does not set; CVE-2026-97689 (unbounded chunk
# allocation) is a DoS against pip's own index downloads on a single-tenant
# worker that already runs repo-controlled code. pip 26.2.2 still vendors
# 2.7.0 - clears when a pip release re-vendors urllib3 >= 2.8.0.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
